This repository is a fork of AlexFurina's TWRP device tree for the Samsung Galaxy
A8 2018, android_device_samsung_jackpotlte, branch android-12.1, commit e0531ef.
https://github.com/AlexFurina/android_device_samsung_jackpotlte
The tree's history goes back to Gabriel2392 (Gabriel260), with commits by
AlexFurina, ExtremeXT, adeilmazk and micky387; the git log lists them. The
build files carry the Android Open Source Project Apache License 2.0 header.

Files written for this repository are licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (see LICENSE): vendorsetup.sh, patch-check.ps1,
recovery-inspect.ps1, release.sh and test-notes.md. Our changes to
BoardConfig.mk, device.mk, mkboot/bootimg.mk and
recovery/root/init.recovery.samsungexynos7885.rc are under the same license;
the git log shows them.

Parts from others keep their own authors and licenses:

* Device tree files from the fork (Android.mk, AndroidProducts.mk,
  BoardConfig.mk, device.mk, twrp_jackpotlte.mk, system.prop,
  mkboot/bootimg.mk, recovery/root/*)
  AlexFurina, Gabriel2392 and the contributors above. The build files are
  under the Apache License 2.0 (AOSP header). The files in recovery/root are
  Android Open Source Project and TWRP configuration files (init and ueventd
  scripts, event-log-tags, task_profiles.json, VINTF manifests) adapted for
  this device, Apache License 2.0.

* prebuilt/Image, prebuilt/dtb
  Linux kernel 4.4.302 for the Exynos 7885 and its device tree, built by
  AlexFurina ("Linux version 4.4.302 (Furina@Love) ... Sat Oct 18 00:00:00
  KST 2025"), taken unmodified from the fork. GPL-2.0. The kernel is based on
  Samsung's SM-A530F kernel source, published at
  https://opensource.samsung.com. The exact source has been requested from
  the author: https://github.com/AlexFurina/android_device_samsung_jackpotlte/issues/1

* mkboot/mkbootimg
  Prebuilt x86-64 mkbootimg with Samsung --dt support, taken unmodified from
  the fork. Android Open Source Project tool, Apache License 2.0.

* Flashlight bridge in init.recovery.samsungexynos7885.rc
  The approach (a /tmp directory with max_brightness and a brightness link to
  the Samsung flash node) follows saadelasfur's
  orangefox_device_samsung_m52xq, branch fox_12.1. No files copied.
  https://github.com/saadelasfur/orangefox_device_samsung_m52xq

* patch-check.ps1 (class FoxLzma) and recovery-inspect.ps1 (class
  FoxInspectLzma): the LZMA decoder
  Ported to C# from LzmaSpec.cpp, the reference LZMA decoder by Igor Pavlov,
  which is in the public domain.

* OrangeFox Recovery / TWRP
  The recovery is built from OrangeFox fox_12.1 (based on TWRP), licensed
  under GPL-3.0-or-later. Our changes to it are published in patches/ under
  the same license.
